# archive/wayback holds byte-faithful preserved originals (HTML, images,
# downloads) fetched directly from Wayback/Common Crawl. Their SHA-1 hashes
# are recorded in archive/meta/manifest.json at fetch time, and verify.ts
# checks committed bytes against those hashes. Without this, Git's line-ending
# normalization (core.autocrlf on Windows, or a repo-level text=auto default)
# silently rewrites \r\n to \n on commit for anything it guesses is text,
# corrupting the preserved copy relative to what was actually captured.
# Treating this entire tree as binary disables that normalization outright.
archive/wayback/** -text -diff
